cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "desktop_app_source_updater: A dependency-free source updater for packaged Python desktop applications"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yue
    family-names: Zhao
    affiliation: "University of Rochester, Rochester, NY, USA"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-5012"
abstract: >-
  A small standard-library-only updater that lets an installed Python desktop
  application update its own source code without reinstallation. The
  application ships a stable launcher alongside updateable source files; at
  startup the updater checks a GitHub Release asset, validates the asset's
  manifest and file hashes, and replaces only approved runtime source files
  before the application package is imported. It discovers the newest release
  through GitHub's ordinary redirect for the latest release rather than the
  REST API, so routine startup checks do not consume API quota, and end users
  need neither Git nor a Python installation. It was written to solve a
  recurring problem in scientific laboratories, where software is installed on
  shared computers that the maintainer cannot revisit to apply a fix.
repository-code: "https://github.com/yzhaoinuw/desktop_app_source_updater"
license: MIT
version: 0.3.0
keywords:
  - software updates
  - desktop application
  - Python packaging
  - software deployment
  - research software
# Zenodo concept DOI. It resolves to the newest release, so it stays correct
